<div class="col-xs-12">
  <h1>Rules &amp; Scoring</h1>

  <h2>Scoring</h2>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Football</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>All Players</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% Nfl::ScoringMap.const_get(:MAPPING).each do |statdata, points| %>
            <tr><td><%= statdata.name %></td><td><%= sprintf "%.2f", points %></td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Defense</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% Nfl::ScoringMap.const_get(:DEFENSE_OVERRIDE_MAPPING).each do |statdata, points| %>
            <tr><td><%= statdata.name %></td><td><%= sprintf "%.2f", points %></td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Kickers</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% Nfl::ScoringMap.const_get(:KICKING_OVERRIDE_MAPPING).each do |statdata, points| %>
            <tr><td><%= statdata.name %></td><td><%= sprintf "%.2f", points %></td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Best and Bust*</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Perfect Time (0 sec.)</td><td>2.80</td></tr>
          <tr><td>&frac12; Time (7 sec.)</td><td>1.40</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Over Time (14 sec.+)</td><td>0.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        * Correct answers to best and bust questions are worth a maximum of 2.80 points each.
        Your time for answering the question is recorded. The timer counts down from 14.0
        seconds by 0.1 seconds. The actual points for each question is a formula based on
        the actual time. Three examples are shown here, but almost any value between 2.80 and
        0.00 is possible.
      </p>


    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Baseball</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Batters</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
        <% Mlb::ScoringMap.new.to_h(batter).each do |statdata, points| %>
            <tr><td><%= statdata.name %></td><td><%= sprintf "%.2f", points %></td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Pitchers</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <% %w(era ip k ha bb).each do |name| %>
            <tr><td><%= st(name, Mlb) %></td><td><%= sprintf "%.2f", Mlb::SCORING_MULTIPLIER.(name, :pitcher) %></td></tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Pitcher Bonus</th>
            <th>Points Per Game</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Win</td><td>4.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Save</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Complete Game</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Shutout</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>No Hitter</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Perfect Game</td><td>2.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <!-- league picks have been temporarily disabled
      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>League Pick</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Home Run by Your Pick</td><td>3.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      -->

      <table class="table table-bordered stat-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Best and Bust*</th>
            <th>Points Each</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Perfect Time (0 sec.)</td><td>2.80</td></tr>
          <tr><td>&frac12; Time (7 sec.)</td><td>1.40</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Over Time (14 sec.+)</td><td>0.00</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>
        * Correct answers to best and bust questions are worth a maximum of 2.80 points each.
        Your time for answering the question is recorded. The timer counts down from 14.0
        seconds by 0.1 seconds. The actual points for each question is a formula based on
        the actual time. Three examples are shown here, but almost any value between 2.80 and
        0.00 is possible.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Basketball</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>Not yet implemented</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Hockey</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>Not yet implemented</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>How to play</h2>
  <desc>In addition to our Terms &amp; Conditions, contests at Sportsbeep are governed by the following set of rules:</desc>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Pick a Game</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>
        This is how you enter a Sportsbeep contest. Pick a live, upcoming MLB game to enter your ticket for the contest.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Your Ticket</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>
        Players.  Pitcher, Catcher, Corner Infielder (First and Third), Middle Infielder (Second and Short), Outfielder.
      </p>
      <!-- league picks have been temporarily disabled
      <p>
        League Pick.  Pick a team playing at the same time as the game you picked or shortly thereafter.
        This is a limited list of concurrent or upcoming games from which you can pick a team.  That team's home runs will
        contribute to your overall score for this contest, even though it's a different game.  The object is to pick the
        team you believe will score the most home runs.  This is designed to give a contest at least one element that is
        completely unrelated to the two teams in the contest.
      </p>
      -->
      <p>
        Picking a Pool.  Right now, it's only "Play for Free."  Once you pick a pool, your ticket is submitted.  The timed
        best/best questions come next.  It's important to note that to prevent someone from "sampling" the best and bust questions,
        backing out, and then trying again for better questions, the ticket is committed before you see the questions.  This means
        that if your battery dies, you lose network connection, etc. before completely answering the questions, you'll get 0 points
        for the questions but the ticket is committed anyway.
      </p>
      <p>
        Best/Bust Questions.  These are 6 prediction questions that have only two answers: one team or the other that is playing
        in the game on which the contest is based.  The first three are "BEST" questions, which ask you to predict which team will
        be the BEST at a particular stat (singles, home runs, strike outs, etc.).  The second three are "BUST".  Points are awarded
        for the right answer and the time you take to answer each question.  Answering correctly is only part of the scoring.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your ticket’s total score will be a combination of Sportsbeep fantasy points from the players picked for
        each position on your roster <!-- , home runs from the team you picked as the League Pick,-->
        and your answers and times for the Best &amp; Bust questions.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Contests</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>
        Regardless of how many people enter a ticket for the game live MLB game, contests are always 10 tickets.  If 100 tickets
        are entered, they will be organized into 10 contests of 10 tickets.  This is done randomly.  If a ticket is not filled,
        “house players” with zero points will be assumed.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="collapsed">
    <header><h3>Winners (future)</h3></header>
    <div class="collapsed-content">
      <p>
        For each contests, 7 out of the 10 people win. Tickets are scored and the top 7 people win. First
        place almost doubles their money. Seventh place breaks even. The exact payouts are as follows (payout
        dollar value of the entry fee):
      </p>
      <table class="table table-bordered">
        <tr><td>1st</td><td>$1.909</td></tr>
        <tr><td>2nd</td><td>$1.545</td></tr>
        <tr><td>3rd</td><td>$1.364</td></tr>
        <tr><td>4th</td><td>$1.136</td></tr>
        <tr><td>5th</td><td>$1.090</td></tr>
        <tr><td>6th</td><td>$1.045</td></tr>
        <tr><td>7th</td><td>$1.000</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="spacer"></div>

</div>
